from pathlib import Path
p=Path('outputs/README.md'); s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
s=s.replace('## Files','## Your uploaded response file\nThe supplied export has 70 rows and includes year, branch, CGPA range, technical-skill confidence, preparation frequency, internship/project experience, placement confidence, and expected salary range. It does **not** include a support-priority question. The app now recognizes the confidence question wording in this export and charts salary expectations when support-priority answers are absent. Do not report support needs from this dataset.\n\n## Files')
s=s.replace('`google_form_questionnaire.md` — the survey wording and privacy reminder.','`google_form_questionnaire.md` — the questions visible in the supplied response export and the fields available for analysis.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
Path('outputs/google_form_questionnaire.md').write_text('''# Questions in the supplied response export\n\nThis reference is based on the column headings in `Dma lab  - Form responses 1.csv`. The export contains these survey questions:\n\n1. What is your current year of study?\n2. Which broad branch/group are you in?\n3. CGPA range\n4. How confident are you in your job-related technical skills? (1–5)\n5. How regularly are you preparing for placements? (1–5)\n6. Have you completed an internship or substantial industry project?\n7. How confident are you that you can secure a suitable placement? (1–5)\n8. What salary range do you currently expect for your first job?\n\nThe exported file does not contain a question about students’ top support priority. The app therefore cannot calculate that result from these responses; it displays salary-range counts instead. The data describes student self-reports and does not include actual job-offer outcomes.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
